            <div xml:id="d716">

                <pb facs="0816" n="723" xml:id="pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.516/363: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chapin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-17T13:00:00-05:00">May 17, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. Chamber of Deputies this morning unanimously passed without serious
                    discussion and without modification bill authorizing Government to sign revised
                    contract for purchase of Banque Nationale. Text of bill and contract is the
                    final one forwarded by de la Rue and received here Sunday, a copy of which it is
                    understood was communicated to the Department.</p>
                <p>Am informed that bill will come up in Senate probably Tuesday where no opposition
                    is of course expected.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
